                <h3 style="margin-top: 0; color: #27ae60;">Executive Summary</h3>
                <p>Analysis of 20,058 Lichess games reveals that <strong>White's first-move advantage is real but modest (52.3%)</strong>, while <strong>rating differential has a dominant effect on outcomes</strong>. The higher-rated player wins 65.3% overall, rising to 87.5% when the gap exceeds 500 points.</p>
